{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>In the Book of the Wars of YHWH.</b> It was a book on its own, and there the wars of YHWH on behalf of those who fear Him are written. It is possible that it was from the days of Abraham, for many books have been lost and are not found among us, like the words of Nathan and Gad and the Chronicles of the Kings of Israel and the songs of Solomon and his proverbs." "<b>Et Vahev in Sufah.</b> Wars took place in ancient times in the places mentioned, and there והב is not in the language of the holy tongue, and likewise ופסי and שתי and יזתא, and also ושני — or the meaning of ושני is that the vav is for joining, and all this because a vav as a root letter is not found at the beginning of a word, except the word ווי העמודים, though you will find it in place of yod, as in ולד, and the meaning of the translator [Targum] in Aramaic is known."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:18:40.599950002Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}